  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly points to scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted as the best configuration (config_024, 0.725 acc). The only major untested design axis is the RNA encoder: scgpt has not been evaluated in any completed experiment. Config_041 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) directly tests whether the more expressive scgpt encoder can push accuracy beyond 0.725 in the already-validated best architecture. This is the highest-information experiment: if scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, we gain a new best and can exploit it in the remaining 3 slots; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as optimal and can spend remaining budget on minor fusion/aggregation refinements. Expected relative cost: scgpt is a larger generative encoder than scvi_n200, so I estimate ~5–7 GPU hours (moderately above config_024's 3.60 h but well within budget), making it a reasonable investment given the potential accuracy gain."
}

